<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">defeat</ansi>

When your leader falls, the world rarely leaves your company where it lay.
Most defeats end in one of four situations, picked by what beat you and
where. <ansi fg="yellow">No level is lost</ansi> in any of them: the cost is the trouble you wake
into. No game time passes (<ansi fg="command">help death</ansi> for the rest).

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Rescued</ansi>
A passing traveller carries your company to the nearest settlement: one in
the zone where you fell, otherwise the church you would have woken in.
Every member wakes Hungry and Exhausted, so eat and rest before the next
road (<ansi fg="command">help survival</ansi>).

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Captured</ansi> (by people)
Your company wakes in the captors' camp, the leader bound for a few
moments and unable to move. Your pack and most of your gold are locked in
a chest there, guarded by a weak group; about a quarter of your gold is gone
for good. What you wear is not taken. Defeat the guards, then
<ansi fg="command">reclaim</ansi> the chest in that room. Walk away without it and it stays
held, saved with your character, until you come back. Guards you have not
beaten are back over the chest when you return; those you beat stay down.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Left for dead</ansi> (by beasts and the undead)
You wake where you fell. The foes, and anything else hostile there, have
gone for a while. Each member of your company who was with you
carries a lasting wound, a fifth of their health
held back until it is treated or rested away (<ansi fg="command">help wounds</ansi>).

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Robbed</ansi> (by people)
You wake where you fell, the foes gone, a fifth of your gold and a share of
your loose goods taken for good. Worn gear, quest items, keys and camp
gear are never taken, and nothing taken is held anywhere.

Gold in the bank is never touched by a capture or a robbery. Characters of
level 5 and below are never captured or robbed, so a new company loses no
goods to a defeat.

When nothing fits (a world with no scenarios, or a defeat the table does
not cover) you wake at the last city's church a level down, as
<ansi fg="command">help death</ansi> describes. Companions who die in the fight can still be
raised at a church or shaman wherever you wake: <ansi fg="command">help resurrect</ansi>.

<ansi fg="yellow">Usage:</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">reclaim</ansi>
  In the capture room, with its guards down, take back the pack and gold
  the captors held. Elsewhere it tells you where they are held.

The Company panel's Inventory tab shows what is held and where.
